// The marketplace on Cloudflare (Workers static assets — what Cloudflare now calls Pages), 20-Sep-2026.
// The `assets` block serves web/dist-market as-is: every request is a static-asset request (free and
// unlimited on the Free plan) EXCEPT the three prefixes in run_worker_first, which reach the script in
// workers/market.js first (release R6, 24-Sep-2026):
//   /api/*     the same-origin catalog (/api/market[?ref=]) — the Render origin through the Cache API:
//              fresh 60 s, stale-while-revalidate, the last good copy when the origin is cold or down
//   /assets/*  a missing chunk is a real 404 (no-store) instead of index.html + "immutable"
//   /fonts/*   same
// `single-page-application` still returns index.html with HTTP 200 for any other path that is not a
// file (the old Vercel rewrite); response headers for static files come from public/_headers, copied
// into the build root by Vite. The Worker sets its own headers on what it answers itself.
// Budget: only run_worker_first requests count against Workers Free (100k/day) — see workers/market.js.
// Deploy: python -m scripts.deploy_cf market (builds first) or .github/workflows/cf-deploy.yml; a
// release uploads a version and switches traffic with `wrangler versions deploy` (docs/RELEASE.md),
// so a rollback is the previous version @100%.
// `routes` with custom_domain attach the hostnames: wrangler creates the DNS records and the
// certificate in the zone (same account) on deploy.
{
  "name": "yq-marketplace",
  "main": "workers/market.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-18",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist-market",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "not_found_handling": "single-page-application",
    "run_worker_first": ["/api/*", "/assets/*", "/fonts/*"]
  },
  "routes": [
    { "pattern": "yqmarketplace.com", "custom_domain": true },
    { "pattern": "www.yqmarketplace.com", "custom_domain": true }
  ],
  "workers_dev": true,
  // Workers Logs (free tier: 200k events/day, 3-day retention): the Worker logs one line per origin
  // timeout/error and nothing per hit, so the volume is tiny and a cold-origin day is visible.
  "observability": { "enabled": true }
}
